# Architect thinking — Gates + Routing

Deep patterns live in **`.cursor/skills/architect-thinking/`** (on-demand). This rule stays auto-attached for tiered delivery + repository discipline only.

## Tiered solution approach (mandatory)

For every bug, issue, JIRA, analysis, or enhancement — after analysis emit a full **OPTIONS BOARD** (**L0 + L1 + L2 + L3**). Do not end with evidence-only / single next-step when code options exist. `N/A — <one line>` only when a tier truly does not apply.

| Tier | When | Effort / risk |
|------|------|----------------|
| **L0 Hotfix** | Smallest safe change — config/flag/guard. No schema/lib. Deploy today. | Hours / low |
| **L1 Proper fix** | Root cause within existing code/framework. | ~1 day / medium |
| **L2 Enhancement** | Schema, index, config, new topic. Planned release. | Days |
| **L3 Architectural** | Framework upgrade, outbox, circuit breaker, cross-module. | Weeks |

Full examples and L3 seeds: `.cursor/skills/architect-thinking/tiered-solutions.md`. Planning engine: `00-workspace-core.md` § Post-analysis OPTIONS BOARD + autopilot directive.

## Repository layer — no comments

Do **not** add narrative/doc comments in `**/repository/**/*.java` (or equivalent DAO repository interfaces). Prefer clear method names and query text. Details: `repository-no-comments.md`.

